# Question: does a running Ze daemon refuse a configured SSH public key when
# the account's login-service set excludes ssh while admitting the same key
# for an account whose set includes ssh (and admitting the excluded account on
# REST)?
# Why a unit test cannot decide it: SSH public-key authentication bypasses
# ChainAuthenticator and calls CheckLoginService directly from the wish
# PublicKeyAuth callback; only a real SSH handshake against a running daemon
# proves that callback is wired to the accepted login-service generation.
#
# VALIDATES: AC-2 -- SSH public-key authentication honors login-service sets
# PREVENTS: public-key logins bypassing the password-path login-service gate

option=timeout:value=45s
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture plugin/login-service-ssh-publickey $PORT $PORT2:timeout=40s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=OK: configured SSH public key refused when ssh is excluded
expect=stderr:contains=OK: configured SSH public key admitted when ssh is included
reject=stderr:contains=ZE-OBSERVER-FAIL
